WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.990
Elon Musk has spelled out numerous doomsday
scenarios for the 7.9 billion people on our

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.900
planet: the threat of AI, asteroids, climate change.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:15.240
Yet he believes one of the greatest risks
to civilization is our population collapsing.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.200
This is what he said at the Wall Street Journal’s
CEO Council Summit in December.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.810
If we don't have more children, civilization
is going to crumble.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.550
Mark my words.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:33.150
That’s the polar opposite of headlines over
the years that have warned there are too many people.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:38.260
Stanford biologist Paul Ehrlich wrote in his
1968 best-selling book The Population Bomb:

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.649
“In the 1970s, hundreds of millions of people
will starve to death” due to overpopulation

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:45.109
which didn’t happen.

00:00:45.109 --> 00:00:49.600
At that time, the world’s population was
growing quickly, increasing by 2.1 per cent

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.989
a year on average.

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:54.199
However, it has since slowed down, falling
by half.

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:59.059
To the point where the United Nations predicts
the world’s population will virtually stop

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:05.500
growing by the end of the century, reaching
10.9 billion people by 2100.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.960
Even that estimate is too high for some.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.840
Musk has called it “utter nonsense” and
only the “best case” scenario.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:17.310
Norwegian academic Jorgan Randers believes
the population will peak at 8 billion in 2040

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.689
and decline from there.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.070
The fall in population growth is largely due
to falling fertility rates.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.990
In the year 1800, the average American woman
had seven kids.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.229
By 1900, that dropped to 3.5.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:32.530
Today, it’s 1.64 children.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:38.310
That’s below the replacement rate of 2.1
- the level at which births balance deaths.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.780
Meaning not enough babies are born for a generation
to replace itself.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.380
People in richer countries tend to have fewer
kids.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.920
Urbanization has reduced the need for children
to work on farms.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.749
There’s greater access to contraception.

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:54.490
And more women are establishing careers before
starting a family.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:59.749
However, the birth rate is even low for some
middle-income countries like Brazil, Thailand,

00:01:59.749 --> 00:02:00.999
and Chile

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:06.130
Even populous India has dropped below the
replacement level to 2.0 and in cities, it’s

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.130
even less.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:11.190
In fact, the only region with strong population
growth is Africa.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.890
So what will a low birth rate mean?

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.280
Fewer people make and consume less stuff.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.980
There will be fewer new homes and schools.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.050
Less demand for services such as restaurants
and shops.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.510
Your standard of living could be impacted
as facilities are cut back.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.890
Mass transit depends on high demand.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:33.350
Fewer people on buses and in subways will
mean less money to maintain the infrastructure,

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.810
which could translate into longer wait times
and fewer routes.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.820
Military strength could decline.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:44.660
As demographer Lyman Stone once said: “You
need warm bodies to fill the uniforms.”

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.370
Some observers predict dire consequences.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:52.710
Jonathan Last, author of What to Expect When
No One’s Expecting, warns if people in authoritarian

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.710
societies have more children than citizens
of liberal democracies, “over the long haul,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.960
those people inherit the earth” leading
to chaos and instability.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.450
At the same time that fertility rates are
falling, people are living longer.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.060
Older people are making up a bigger share
of the total population.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.000
Nearly all areas of the world are experiencing
aging - shown in dark blue.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.050
A small number of workers will be left to
support many retirees.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.400
This is an extreme example of what that could
look like.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.680
It resembles an inverted population pyramid
where there are too few working-age people

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.710
supporting too many elderly.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:30.230
This wild imbalance could cause governments
to raise taxes to cover the burden of caring

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.230
for seniors.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:36.410
In 2019, there were three workingage people
for each elderly person in Europe and North

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:37.410
America.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.160
By 2050, that’s projected to fall below
two.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.690
And in some countries, it already has.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:47.320
Japan is grappling with a labor shortage by
having robots care for the elderly in some

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.510
nursing homes.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:54.550
To entice more people to have kids, the Japanese
government pays parents 100,000 yen or $876

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.590
dollars per baby.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:00.260
Do it for Denmark.
A tongue-in-cheek campaign by a Danish travel

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:05.430
agency in 2014 urged people to go on more
vacation to get knocked up as stats showed

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.900
Danes had more sex on holidays.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.440
In the European Union, the fertility rate
is a mere 1.53 births per woman.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.210
Iran is so worried about its low birth rate
that in 2020, public hospitals and clinics

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.470
stopped offering vasectomies and handing out
contraceptives.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.690
China may be the most populous country, but
its birth rate has been plummeting despite

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:38.250
the government scrapping the controversial
one-child policy in 2016.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:43.890
That got replaced by a two-child policy and
now, families are allowed to have up to three children.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:48.800
Then there’s the possibility of synthetic
wombs to try to encourage people to have more kids.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.230
Scientists have already successfully grown
a baby sheep in what looks like a jumbo-sized

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.420
Ziploc bag.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:58.660
Dutch researchers believe they are within
ten years of creating artificial wombs to

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.540
keep premature babies alive.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:05.790
Sahil Lavingia, the founder of the e-commerce
platform Gumroad, suggested artificial wombs

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.840
would make having kids easier.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.710
Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin added
women’s salaries could increase, as statistics

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.670
show their earnings drop significantly after giving birth.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.930
They discussed this in response to Musk’s
tweet about his population concerns.

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:24.980
The SpaceX CEO says he’s trying to practice
what he preaches by having a lot of kids - six

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.660
boys so far!

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.440
His rocket company wants to build a city on Mars.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.550
However, Musk warns that if there aren’t
enough people on Earth, there definitely won’t

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:36.380
be enough people for the red planet.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.260
Parents are now heavily invested in their
kids, giving them the best shot at a decent life.

